  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [\"navigate a navigable\" algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate), step 22.5, states:\r\n\r\n> If url [matches about:blank](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#matches-about:blank) or is [about:srcdoc](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#about:srcdoc), then:\r\n\r\nI believe this should probably be \"matches about:srcdoc\" instead of \"is about:srcdoc\", as there's a [specific algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#matches-about:srcdoc) for that.",
